A||||3||btoth||Tire Pressure Question||||1||
Z||000000||btoth||06-11-2001||04:13 PM||||I'm looking for some info on what I should have my tire pressure set to.  The tires are BFGoodrich Comp TA VR4s.  Stock 205/60/15 and 215/60/15 for an 86 GT.  I've been running them at the OEM specs of 30 PSI front and rear for almost two years now and haven't noticed any unusual wear.  The tires have a max PSI rating of 44.  I couldn't find any specs from BFGoodrich and the oil changing places always want to pump them up to 35 (which messes with my handling since it was aligned at 30).  Just wondering if any of you would recommend changing the pressure.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bruce||06-11-2001||04:15 PM||||I have the BF Goodrich Comp T/A's, and I keep the pressure at 32 psi. I get good handling and no tread deviations.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||06-11-2001||06:11 PM||||BF touring TA's  205 55 15 frt @ 22psi<BR>BF touring TA's  215 60 15 rear @ 32 psi  <P>I found I like softer frt tires to ease the ride and still no low tire buldge or uneven tread wear.  I find the frt sticks better.||||reg||1
Z||000003||btoth||06-11-2001||08:01 PM||||So I'm probably fine with the 30 psi as long as the tires don't bulge too much and doesn't look flat.  Thanks for the info!||||reg||1
